    "title": "Safety Service Patrol member killed in collision while helping driver on I-95: Police - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Gabby Allen ,\n4 hours ago\nPRINCE WILLIAM COUNTY, Va. ( DC News Now ) — Virginia State Police (VSP) said a Department of Transportation (VDOT) contractor was killed in a collision along Interstate 95 on Saturday night.\nJust before 8 p.m., the Safety Service Patrol (SSP) member was helping a disabled Audi on the right shoulder of the interstate at the 151-mile marker. That’s when VSP said a Chrysler 300 Sedan lost control, crossed all lanes of travel and struck the patroller, as well as the Audi driver.\nCar rollover closes street in Alexandria The patroller was taken to a nearby hospital, where he later died. In an update Wednesday, police identified him as Michael Freeland, 48, of Falls Church.\nThe Audi driver suffered serious, but non-life-threatening injuries.\nVSP said authorities are discussing the case with the Prince William County Commonwealth’s Attorney’s Office to determine potential charges. The crash remains under investigation.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WFXRtv.",
